involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n2712,RECIÉN NACIDO,\"The term \"\"recién nacido\"\" refers to newborns, particularly in the context of their medical care and nutritional needs during the early days of life. Newborns are individuals whose gastrointestinal tracts are exposed to a variety of microorganisms at the time of birth, which plays a significant role in the development of their microbiota. This exposure is crucial for establishing a healthy gut flora, which can impact their overall health and development in the subsequent days and weeks.\",15\r\n2550,SMOFLIPID,\"SMOFLIPID is a brand of lipid emulsion specifically designed for parenteral nutrition. It is formulated as a 20% lipid emulsion that combines soybean oil, medium-chain triglycerides, olive oil, and fish oil, creating a balanced mixture aimed at providing a more physiological composition for nutritional support. This fat emulsion is particularly beneficial for intravenous nutrition in newborns, as it supplies essential fatty acids and calories necessary for their growth and development. Notably, SMOFLIPID is recognized for its high concentration of alpha-tocopherol and is rich in docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) and eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA), which are important components for overall health.\",13\r\n2549,LIPOFUNDINA,\"LIPOFUNDINA is a brand of lipid emulsion specifically designed for use in parenteral nutrition. It is a 20% fat emulsion that combines soybean oil and medium-chain triglycerides, which enhances tolerance, particularly in newborns. This mixed lipid preparation, introduced in the late 1980s, consists of a balanced formulation of 50% medium-chain triglycerides and 50% long-chain triglycerides derived from soybean oil. LIPOFUNDINA serves to meet the lipid requirements in pediatric nutrition, making it a vital component in intravenous nutrition therapies.\",11\r\n2647,RECIÉN NACIDOS PREMATUROS,\"\"\"RECIÉN NACIDOS PREMATUROS\"\" refers to newborns who are born before 37 weeks of gestation. These infants require special attention in terms of their feeding and care due to their physiological immaturity. They are at risk of undernutrition and therefore need specific nutritional support to ensure their health and development.\",11\r\n2735,LIPOPLUS,\"LIPOPLUS is a specialized fat emulsion designed for intravenous nutrition, primarily utilized in parenteral nutrition. It contains a blend of soybean oil, medium-chain triglycerides, and fish oil, which together provide essential fatty acids necessary for patient care. Additionally, LIPOPLUS is recognized as a fourth-generation lipid emulsion that incorporates omega-3 fatty acids, offering potential anti-inflammatory and hepatoprotective effects. The formulation is particularly beneficial in pediatric nutrition, where it combines fish oil with other lipid components to meet the nutritional needs of young patients. Overall, LIPOPLUS serves as a comprehensive solution for delivering vital lipids in various clinical settings.\",9\r\n2020,INSUFICIENCIA HEPÁTICA,\"Insuficiencia hepática, or hepatic insufficiency, is a severe medical condition characterized by the liver's inability to perform its normal functions. This condition necessitates urgent medical care and careful management of various dietary factors. Specifically, individuals with hepatic insufficiency require specific dietary adjustments, including limited intake of copper and manganese, as well as careful management of lipid intake, particularly in cases involving parenteral nutrition. Furthermore, this condition can significantly impact the metabolism of nutrients, especially in newborns, highlighting the critical nature of liver function in overall nutritional status and metabolic processes.\",7\r\n14703,CLINOLEIC,\"Clinoleic is a 20% lipid emulsion utilized in parenteral nutrition, specifically formulated to deliver essential fatty acids. It is composed of a blend of soybean oil and olive oil, introduced in the late 1990s. Clinoleic is notable for its high content of oleic acid and vitamin E, which contribute to its nutritional benefits. As a third-generation lipid emulsion, it is enriched with olive oil, recognized for its high antioxidant content and its resistance to lipid peroxidation, making it a valuable option in clinical settings for patients requiring parenteral nutrition.\",5\r\n2736,COLESTASIS,\"Coleostasis is a medical condition characterized by impaired bile flow from the liver to the duodenum. This condition can occur in newborns and is often associated with parenteral nutrition, which is a method of feeding that bypasses the gastrointestinal tract. The inability of bile to flow properly can significantly impact the nutritional status of affected individuals, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing this condition in clinical settings.\",4\r\n2718,BALANCE HIDROELECTROLÍTICO,\"BALANCE HIDROELECTROLÍTICO refers to the critical process of monitoring and managing the hydroelectrolytic balance in patients, particularly those receiving parenteral nutrition. This balance is essential for maintaining fluid and electrolyte levels, which are vital for overall health. The importance of this management is especially pronounced in vulnerable populations, such as newborns, where precise control of these levels is crucial for their well-being.\",2\r\n15548,OMEGAVEN,\"Omegaven is a lipid solution made exclusively from fish oil, designed to effectively treat specific conditions in pediatric patients. It is particularly beneficial for individuals suffering from liver disease related to parenteral nutrition, with a notable efficacy in those affected by short bowel syndrome.\",2\r\n2641,ALIMENTACIÓN ENTERAL,\"Alimentación enteral is a method of providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract, primarily utilized when patients are stabilized. This approach is particularly significant for infants, especially those who are premature, as it ensures they receive essential nutrients directly through their digestive system. Alimentación enteral serves as an alternative to parenteral nutrition, offering a means to deliver nutrition effectively through the digestive tract.\",8\r\n10953,OLEIC ACID,,2\r\n14702,TCL INTRALIPID,\"TCL Intralipid is a product derived from soybean oil, used in lipid emulsions for nutritional support, particularly in providing essential fatty acids and influencing inflammatory responses.\",7\r\n2708,ALIMENTACIÓN ENTERAL TOTAL,\"\"\"ALIMENTACIÓN ENTERAL TOTAL\"\" refers to the practice of providing complete nutritional support through enteral feeding, particularly for infants. This approach is designed to ensure that infants receive all necessary nutrients directly through the gastrointestinal tract, thereby supporting their growth and development effectively.\",2\r\n2586,CESÁREA,\"Cesárea, or cesarean section, is a surgical procedure employed to deliver a baby through incisions made in the abdomen and uterus. This method of delivery can have implications for breastfeeding initiation, potentially affecting the early stages of breastfeeding for the newborn. Additionally, cesárea is associated with a distinct microbiota composition in newborns, which is characterized by the presence of skin-related microorganisms. This difference in microbiota may have further implications for the health and development of infants born via cesarean section.\",2\r\n6792,MADRE,\"MADRE refers to the concept of a mother, who plays a crucial role in the development of a newborn's microbiome through close contact during birth and early feeding. This relationship is essential for establishing a healthy microbial environment for the infant. Additionally, in a specific case, the mother of a patient has a history of thyroid crises and is a smoker, which may influence the patient's overall health. This highlights the multifaceted impact a mother can have, not only in nurturing and supporting the newborn's development but also in potentially affecting the health outcomes of older children or patients through her own health behaviors and medical history.\",2\r\n8992,ALIMENTACIÓN SÓLIDA,Alimentación sólida (solid food introduction) marks a significant change in the composition of the intestinal microbiota as the child grows.,1\r\n2715,APORTE PROTEICO-CALÓRICO,Refers to the ideal nutritional intake of proteins and calories necessary for weight gain in newborns.,1\r\n8993,DESTETE,Destete (weaning) is the process that further diversifies the intestinal microbiota as the child transitions to solid foods.,1\r\n2713,FLUIDOS Y ELECTROLITOS,\"Fluids and electrolytes are crucial components for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance in patients, particularly those receiving nutritional support. The management of these elements is especially important in vulnerable populations, such as newborns, where careful monitoring is necessary to prevent complications. Ensuring an appropriate balance of fluids and electrolytes is essential for overall health and recovery in these patients.\",1\r\n8991,LACTANCIA NATURAL,\"Lactancia natural (natural breastfeeding) is a key factor in the development of the newborn's intestinal microbiota, providing a continuous supply of beneficial bacteria.\",1\r\n8990,PARTO NATURAL,Parto natural (natural birth) is associated with the newborn acquiring a microbiota similar to that of the mother's vaginal microbiota.,1\r\n2719,PÉRDIDAS INSENSIBLES DE AGUA,\"Refers to the unavoidable loss of water from the body, particularly significant in newborns due to their skin immaturity.\",1\r\n2720,TEMPERATURA AMBIENTAL,The environmental temperature that can affect the health and hydration needs of newborns.,1\r\n15498,ENTEROCOLITIS NECROSANTE,\"La enterocolitis necrosante es una complicación grave que puede afectar a los recién n